Monaco Editor 0.57.0 embeds DOMPurify 3.4.15 in
esm/vs/base/browser/dompurify/dompurify.js, imported by domSanitize.js.
This source is part of Volli Code's bundled Monaco renderer. It is separate
from Monaco's npm DOMPurify dependency, which resolves to 3.4.16.

The embedded source carries this notice:

/*! @license DOMPurify 3.4.15 | (c) Cure53 and other contributors | Released under the Apache license 2.0 and Mozilla Public License 2.0 | github.com/cure53/DOMPurify/blob/3.4.15/LICENSE */

Volli elects Apache-2.0 for this dual-licensed source, as for the npm
DOMPurify dependency. The full Apache-2.0 and MPL-2.0 license texts are
reproduced in the DOMPurify license group of THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES; those
texts are identical in DOMPurify 3.4.15 and 3.4.16.

Upstream: https://github.com/cure53/DOMPurify/tree/3.4.15
Security follow-up: VC-600. The npm version override does not patch this
embedded source. Refresh this notice when Monaco's embedded source changes.
